ts into the treatment of hypercalcemia and the study of neuroendocrine tumors. As an editor, Kronenberg HM has played a significant role in advancing endocrine research and education, particularly in relation to conditions such as pheochromocytoma and insulinoma. His extensive involvement in the textbook underscores his expertise and commitment to the field of endocrinology.", "MELMED S:Melmed S is a prominent researcher and author in the field of endocrinology, particularly known for his contributions to the understanding and treatment of various endocrine disorders. He has made significant contributions to the literature on the adenohypophysis and the treatment of disorders related to prolactin. Melmed S is notably recognized for his work on acromegaly, having authored clinical practice guidelines for this condition.\n\nHe is one of the authors and editors of the \"Williams Textbook of Endocrinology,\" a comprehensive resource that covers a wide range of topics within endocrinology, including the treatment of osteoporosis and the management of neuroendocrine tumors. His contributions to this textbook have provided valuable insights into various endocrine disorders, including insulinoma and pheochromocytoma. Through his extensive work, Melmed S has established himself as a key figure in the field of endocrinology, influencing both clinical practice and academic research.", "POLONSKY KS:Polonsky KS is a prominent figure in the field of endocrinology, recognized for his significant contributions as both a co-author and editor of the \"Williams Textbook of Endocrinology.\" His work has greatly enhanced the understanding of various hormonal regulations and disorders, including conditions such as insulinoma, osteoporosis, hypercalcemia, and neuroendocrine tumors. As an editor, Polonsky KS has played a crucial role in shaping the content of the textbook, providing insights into endocrine functions and specific conditions like pheochromocytoma. His contributions have established him as a key authority in the field, making the \"Williams Textbook of Endocrinology\" a vital resource for understanding complex endocrine issues.", "TRH:TRH (Thyrotropin-Releasing Hormone) is a hypothalamic factor and a hormone that plays a crucial role in the endocrine system by stimulating the secretion of Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone (TSH) from the pituitary gland.", "HORMONAS DEL EJE HIPOTÁLAMO-HIPÓFISO-TIROIDEO:Hormones of the hypothalamic-pituitary-thyroid axis are involved in the regulation of thyroid function."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}